# Patternflood demos: settings for patternflood.service (firmware/demos/run.py).
# Edit, then: sudo systemctl restart patternflood
#
# The buttons on top, left to right: previous, select, next, sleep. Previous and
# next step through the demos on a shelf; select opens the menu, where previous
# and next (or k1) change shelf, k0 picks the demo and k3 sets brightness. Select
# or a click on any knob closes it.

# Which demos the menu offers: empty for all, shelves comma-separated (patternflow,community-1to1,community,patternflood,audio,cable),
# or "upstream" for SeungHun's 48 presets alone. Those are native code, so they run far
# faster on a Pi Zero than our numpy demos: on the Zero W use PF_ONLY=upstream.
PF_ONLY=
# Demo to start on, by name or index within PF_ONLY's list
# (see: python3 /opt/patternflood/demos/run.py --only "$PF_ONLY" --list).
PF_DEMO=0
# Frame rate to aim for. The Pi 5 holds 60 on all but the heaviest demos (Helix, Moon: high 50s);
# a Pi Zero W falls well short of 30.
PF_FPS=60
# Starting brightness, 0..1 (k3 changes it in the menu).
PF_BRIGHT=0.3
# Knobs: i2c[:BUS] (the 4991 chain on the header), or none.
PF_KNOBS=i2c:1
# Buttons: gpio (the four on top, via the gpio-key overlay in config.txt), or none.
PF_BUTTONS=gpio
# Frames: udp[:IP], straight to the card on this Pi's Ethernet.
PF_OUT=udp:192.168.75.39
# Audio for the visualizers: none, alsa[:DEVICE] or pulse[:SOURCE]. The box has no microphone yet.
PF_AUDIO=none
